===============================================================================
NOTICE - MODIFICATIONS IN THIS FORK
===============================================================================

This fork extends the original CNKI Metadata Exporter with the following
additions. Attribution of the original work is unchanged: all functionality
present in the upstream project remains the copyright of Yao and is licensed
under the MIT License above.

1. Publication-time range limit per collection
   Each search collection can be restricted to an explicit publication date
   window, and the full time range can still be requested when needed
   (see the --all-time option and the publication_time field). This avoids
   exporting irrelevant records and makes incremental collection reproducible.

2. Automatic date-range splitting beyond the paging cap
   CNKI stops exposing records once a result set grows past roughly 6,000
   items. When a collection exceeds that cap, this fork automatically splits
   its publication time range into smaller sub-ranges and continues crawling
   each slice until all records are exported
   (see the --max-results-per-slice option).

3. Resumable runs with skip-on-repeated-failure
   When a collection fails repeatedly, it is skipped after the retry limit is
   reached instead of blocking the whole job. Already downloaded batches are
   reused on re-run, so an interrupted job resumes where it stopped and the
   remaining collections keep progressing.

Permission note: this NOTICE is provided for attribution and documentation
purposes only. It does not modify, narrow, or add conditions to the MIT
License text above, which continues to govern the use of this software.